---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - English Vocabulary & Idioms">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 17 October 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <h2>Who we are</h2>
                    <p>English Vocabulary &amp; Idioms (package <code>com.logicpathsystems.englishvocabulary</code>) is an Android app published by Logic Path Systems ("we", "us"). This policy explains what information is handled when you use the app and the choices you have.</p>

                    <h2>Information that stays on your device</h2>
                    <p>All vocabulary, examples and quiz questions are built into the app. The following is stored only in the app's private storage on your device and is never sent to us:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>your saved words and up to 30 recently viewed entries;</li>
                        <li>your theme setting;</li>
                        <li>missed quiz questions and up to 20 quiz results (score and date);</li>
                        <li>simple usage counters, such as how many days you have opened the app, used to decide when to ask for a rating.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Android cloud backup is turned off for this data. You can delete it at any time in <strong>Settings → Reset local learning data</strong>, by clearing the app's data in Android settings, or by uninstalling the app.</p>

                    <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
                    <p>The app is free and shows ads provided by Google AdMob: a banner at the bottom of the main screens and app open ads, which may appear when you start or return to the app. To serve, measure and limit ads and to prevent fraud, Google may collect and process:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>your device's advertising ID;</li>
                        <li>your IP address, from which an approximate location can be inferred;</li>
                        <li>device and app information, such as model, operating system, language and app version;</li>
                        <li>how you interact with ads.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Where permitted and where you have agreed, ads may be personalised based on this information. Google acts as an independent controller of this data under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.</p>

                    <h2>Analytics (Google Analytics for Firebase)</h2>
                    <p>We use Google Analytics for Firebase to understand how the app is used so we can improve it. It collects pseudonymous usage data such as an app instance ID, the advertising ID where available, which screens are opened, session length, first open and app updates, device model, operating system, language, and approximate country or region derived from your IP address.</p>
                    <p>We do not send your saved words, quiz answers or anything you look up to Firebase, and we do not collect your name, email address, contacts, precise location or files. Analytics data is kept for the period set in our Google Analytics settings (no longer than 14 months) and then deleted automatically.</p>

                    <h2>Your consent and choices</h2>
                    <p>If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, the app asks for your consent through Google's consent message before ads are personalised and before data is used for these purposes. You can change your choice at any time in <strong>Settings → Privacy choices</strong>.</p>
                    <p>Everywhere, you can reset or delete your advertising ID, or opt out of personalised ads, in your device's Google or Privacy settings. If you decline personalisation you may still see non-personalised ads.</p>

                    <h2>Other features</h2>
                    <p>When you choose to share a word or the app, Android's share sheet sends the text only to the app you pick. The "Rate us" option uses Google Play's in-app review, which is handled by Google Play. The app does not request access to your contacts, camera, microphone, photos, files or precise location. Links to web pages open in your browser and are covered by those sites' policies.</p>

                    <h2>Data security and transfers</h2>
                    <p>Data collected by Google's services is sent over encrypted connections (HTTPS) and may be processed on Google's servers in other countries, protected under Google's data-transfer safeguards. We do not sell your personal information.</p>

                    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
                    <p>Learning data on your device is kept until you reset it in Settings, clear the app's data or uninstall the app. We keep no copy. Advertising data is retained by Google according to Google's policies. Analytics data is automatically deleted after the retention period set in our Google Analytics settings (no longer than 14 months).</p>
                    <p>To ask us to delete analytics data linked to your app instance, email <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a>; we respond within 30 days. You can also reset your advertising ID at any time in your device settings.</p>

                    <h2>Children</h2>
                    <p>The app is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided information through the app, contact us and we will help remove it.</p>

                    <h2>Your rights</h2>
                    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or restrict the use of your personal data, to object to processing, and to withdraw consent. Because we do not hold an account or your learning data, most requests are handled through the controls above or directly by Google. For analytics data linked to your app instance, or any other privacy request, contact us using the details below.</p>

                    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>We may update this policy when the app changes. The latest version is always available in the app and on this page, with the effective date shown above.</p>

                    <h2>Contact</h2>
                    <p><strong>Logic Path Systems</strong><br />Email: <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a></p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
    
    .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content a {
        color: var(--primary);
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .legal-content a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .legal-content code {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        padding: 0.15em 0.4em;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 0.95em;
    }
</style>
